# AUR packages — the half that is not in Arch's own repos.
#
# Same format and the same "not verified against a live mirror" caveat as
# arch/pkglist; see that file's header. install-linux.sh installs these with the
# AUR helper (paru by default) and skips the section entirely if none is found,
# so a machine without an AUR helper still gets everything in pkglist.
#
# Kept separate from pkglist rather than merged and handed wholesale to paru:
# an AUR package builds from source and can prompt, so it is worth seeing which
# of the two lists a failure came from.

# The GitHub CLI's own package is in the repos (gh); these are not.
mist-cli
firebase-tools

# iris — the inline completion overlay. .config/iris is symlinked by the
# installer and .zshrc autostarts it, so this is load-bearing rather than
# optional on a machine that wants the same prompt.
#
# UNVERIFIED, and the most likely thing in this port to be missing: iris is
# distributed on macOS through the author's own Homebrew tap, and whether a
# Linux build exists at all was not checkable from the Mac this was written on.
# If it is not packaged, .zshrc degrades cleanly — the `zcache iris` call is a
# no-op when the binary is absent, so the shell comes up without it rather than
# erroring. Drop this line and the iris section of .zshrc keeps working as a
# no-op; do not paper over it with a `curl | sh` installer, which is what the
# Brewfile comment rejected for the same tool.
iris
